WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.294 --> 00:00:16.796
Mandy looked closer at Leo's writing.

2
00:00:17.997 --> 00:00:19.739
"Can you read this, Vinnie?"

3
00:00:20.299 --> 00:00:20.840
she said.

4
00:00:22.061 --> 00:00:24.143
But Vinnie was looking at the photo.

5
00:00:25.384 --> 00:00:26.605
It was glowing blue.

6
00:00:27.806 --> 00:00:30.388
They were standing where the old man had stood!

7
00:00:31.836 --> 00:00:35.058
A well-dressed woman suddenly walked past the children.

8
00:00:36.219 --> 00:00:37.840
She seemed to be in a rush.

9
00:00:39.081 --> 00:00:43.464
As she hurried toward the cathedral door, something fell from her neck.

10
00:00:44.565 --> 00:00:48.008
It landed softly on the open page of Leo's notebook.

11
00:00:49.189 --> 00:00:50.590
It was a mirror locket.

12
00:00:52.051 --> 00:00:54.753
Mandy noticed the small mirror on the notebook.

13
00:00:54.773 --> 00:00:57.234
"Vinnie, look!"

14
00:00:57.875 --> 00:00:59.316
she whispered excitedly.

15
00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:03.883
She picked up the book and held the mirror to the page.

16
00:01:05.124 --> 00:01:07.046
Now Mandy could read the writing!

17
00:01:07.066 --> 00:01:12.931
"The thoughts and ideas of Leonardo di ser Piero da Vinci!"

18
00:01:13.471 --> 00:01:14.032
she read.

19
00:01:14.052 --> 00:01:17.174
"Leonardo da Vinci!"

20
00:01:17.715 --> 00:01:19.036
the children shouted.

21
00:01:20.177 --> 00:01:24.280
The photo glowed red as they fell down the dark tunnel.

22
00:01:26.422 --> 00:01:28.564
They landed with a thump in the attic.

23
00:01:30.848 --> 00:01:33.449
"Wow, the greatest artist of all time!

24
00:01:34.589 --> 00:01:37.730
It's too bad we didn't get to talk to him more!"

25
00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:38.910
cried Mandy.

26
00:01:38.930 --> 00:01:42.851
"I could tell he was special," said Vinnie.

27
00:01:43.932 --> 00:01:45.432
Mandy rolled her eyes.

28
00:01:45.452 --> 00:01:48.473
"Vinnie! Mandy!

29
00:01:48.873 --> 00:01:49.913
Come downstairs!"

30
00:01:50.453 --> 00:01:51.254
shouted Mom.

31
00:01:52.474 --> 00:01:56.375
The children ran down to their parents, who were still in the kitchen.

32
00:01:56.395 --> 00:01:59.336
"We need to talk," said Mom.

33
00:02:00.860 --> 00:02:03.141
The children sat quietly and listened.

34
00:02:03.161 --> 00:02:07.143
"We're moving again," began Dad.

35
00:02:07.163 --> 00:02:10.024
"The company needs me in California."

36
00:02:10.044 --> 00:02:14.706
"California!" the children shouted together.

37
00:02:14.726 --> 00:02:17.647
"We just moved here!"

38
00:02:18.187 --> 00:02:18.888
said Vinnie.

39
00:02:18.908 --> 00:02:22.129
"I know," said Dad.

40
00:02:22.149 --> 00:02:24.650
"But this can't be helped."

41
00:02:25.810 --> 00:02:29.332
For the next few days, the children were busy packing.

42
00:02:30.732 --> 00:02:33.614
"Kids, would you mind clearing out the attic for me?"

43
00:02:33.975 --> 00:02:35.356
Dad asked one morning.

44
00:02:36.637 --> 00:02:40.220
With heavy hearts Vinnie and Mandy went upstairs.

45
00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:44.383
"I'm sad to leave," cried Mandy.

46
00:02:44.403 --> 00:02:49.847
"Well, at least we got to the end of the album," said Vinnie.

47
00:02:51.269 --> 00:02:52.890
He took the album out again.

48
00:02:54.091 --> 00:02:56.473
Each page had a photo of their travels.

49
00:02:57.674 --> 00:03:02.517
In the pictures the old man was gone, replaced by Vinnie and Mandy.

50
00:03:03.937 --> 00:03:06.138
The objects were not glowing anymore.

51
00:03:06.158 --> 00:03:10.599
"We had some great adventures," said Vinnie.

52
00:03:10.619 --> 00:03:15.040
"And we made many friends," added Mandy.

53
00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:17.981
"What was your favorite journey?"

54
00:03:19.521 --> 00:03:20.962
Vinnie thought for a moment.

55
00:03:20.982 --> 00:03:23.442
"I liked every one.

56
00:03:23.922 --> 00:03:29.164
I learned so much about the world—its different people and their special cultures."

57
00:03:30.424 --> 00:03:32.765
"Me too," agreed Mandy.

58
00:03:32.785 --> 00:03:35.205
"What should we do now?"

59
00:03:35.806 --> 00:03:36.446
asked Vinnie.

60
00:03:37.526 --> 00:03:39.086
The children sat and thought.

61
00:03:40.267 --> 00:03:42.587
"Someone else will be living here, right?"

62
00:03:42.887 --> 00:03:43.588
said Mandy.

63
00:03:43.608 --> 00:03:46.548
"Maybe they'll find this album.

64
00:03:47.689 --> 00:03:50.229
Maybe they'll go on photo travels too."

65
00:03:50.249 --> 00:03:53.070
"Should we leave a note?"

66
00:03:53.550 --> 00:03:54.210
asked Vinnie.

67
00:03:54.230 --> 00:03:56.391
"Great idea!"

68
00:03:56.951 --> 00:03:57.671
Mandy said.

69
00:03:58.752 --> 00:04:02.333
She grabbed a pen and turned to the first page of the album.

70
00:04:02.353 --> 00:04:09.156
"On our first trip to Egypt, a glowing pyramid called to us Mandy wrote.

71
00:04:10.197 --> 00:04:13.518
They finished the note and closed the photo album.

72
00:04:14.619 --> 00:04:17.080
Then they put it in a corner of the attic.

73
00:04:18.501 --> 00:04:21.842
A week later, the family shut the door of their house.

74
00:04:23.043 --> 00:04:25.704
Vinnie and Mandy looked up at the attic window.

75
00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:31.147
Exciting adventures were waiting for whoever would find the album next.

76
00:04:32.269 --> 00:04:36.395
For Vinnie and Mandy, another adventure was about to begin.
